<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner plans additional asset sale.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner plans additional asset sale.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Friday it planned to dispose of additional non-core activities worth around five billion crowns.</p>
<p>The company gave no details of the assets it planned to dispose of.</p>
<p>Earlier, presenting first-quarter results, Kvaerner said it had achieved its target a year ahead of schedule to sell 10 billion crowns of non-core assets, as planned when it acquired British conglomerate Trafalgar House Plc in April last year.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
